 will help guide us in the panel discussion along with an introduction to g
 oal setting and positive self-talk. \nCourse: MED 511\n\nInstructors:\n	Ch
 eryl Goldstein (cgoldste)\n	Do Victor (vdo)\n\nMy Group:\n	Name: EDM\n	Loc
 ation: 1080 Katz\n\nObjectives:\n	Develop a personal PerMS action plan tha
 t identifies key skills and necessary resources for supporting ongoing wel
 l-being and academic success.\n\n	Describe how the consistent application 
 of PerMS contributes to their professional identity as resilient and compa
 ssionate physicians \n\n	Apply self-regulation skills\, such as emotional 
 regulation and self-compassion to manage stress and maintain adaptive ment
 al states during high-pressure medical scenarios.\n	Integrate all three co
 mponents of PerMS (Mastery\, Mindset & Motivation\, and Self-regulation) t
 o address complex medical challenges.\n\nView this event online: https://c
 alendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198745
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198745
