BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[C1] LECTURE: WIHP Module 2:  Treaties\, Rights\, and the UN Decla
 ration on the Rights on Indigenous People
DTSTART:20261019T210000Z
DTEND:20261019T215000Z
DTSTAMP:20260903T235526Z
UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198770@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:\nCourse: MED 511\n\nInstructors:\n	Taylor Turvey (turvey)\n\n
 My Group:\n	Name: EDM\n	Location: 1080 Katz\n\nObjectives:\n	Describe the 
 historical contexts within which the different treaties were established.\
 n	Explain why Indigenous leaders and government officials may have held di
 vergent viewpoints over the meaning and stipulations of Treaties 6\, 7 and
  8.\n	Explain the implications of treaties for Indigenous health in Canada
 .\n	Explain the implications of a ‘medicine chest’ in Treaty 6.\n	Eval
 uate the state’s history honouring its treaty commitments in Western Can
 ada.\n	Describe the status of Indigenous health at a global level.\n	Outli
 ne the basic contents and objectives of UNDRIP.\n	Evaluate the reasons why
  Canada refused to endorse UNDRIP until 2016.\n	Discuss the potential impl
 ications of UNDRIP for the health of Indigenous people.\n	Discuss the inte
 rconnectedness of local\, national\, and international political struggles
  to induce positive social change.\n\nView this event online: https://cale
 ndar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198770
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198770
END:VEVENT
