DTEND:20261109T175000Z
DTSTAMP:20260903T235526Z
UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198804@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:\nCourse: MED 511\n\nInstructors:\n	Aruna Chandran (auchandr)\
 n\nMy Group:\n	Name: EDM\n	Location: 1080 Katz\n\nObjectives:\n	Describe t
 he fundamentals of infection prevention control practice with a focus on: 
 Infection surveillance\; Patient management\; Outbreak investigation.\n	Re
 view IPC routine practices.\n	Describe the various IPC precautions and com
 mon organisms associated with each one.\n\nView this event online: https:/
 /calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198804
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198804
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[C1] TEAM BASED LEARNING: Antimicrobial Review
DTSTART:20261116T150000Z
DTEND:20261116T165000Z
DTSTAMP:20260903T235526Z
UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198809@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:FIRST PERSON IN THE ROOM TO OPEN ZOOM.\nCourse: MED 511\n\nIns
 tructors:\n	Roshan Abraham (jrabraha)\n	Oscar Fernandez Garcia (ofernand)\
 n\nMy Group:\n	Name: TBL 16\n	Location: Katz 1078\n\nObjectives:\n	Identif
 y the common pathogens implicated in community acquired pneumonia (CAP).\n
 	Discuss antibiotic regimens appropriate for patients presenting with CAP 
 in the absence of any compelling or aggravating clinical features.\n	Disti
 nguish between cystitis and pyelonephritis with respect to pathophysiology
  and presentation.\n	Distinguish between asymptomatic bacteriuria and UTI\
 , and recognize when urine culture testing should be ordered.\n	Identify t
 he common organisms implicated in urinary tract infections.\n	Discuss firs
 t and second line agents in the treatment of cystitis.\n	Discuss the first
  and second-line agents in the treatment of pyelonephritis.\n	Apply point 
 of care mobile applications for the diagnosis and management of common inf
 ectious diseases.\n\nView this event online: https://calendar.med.ualberta
 .ca/events/198809
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198809
END:VEVENT
