UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198844@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:\nCourse: MED 511\n\nMy Group:\n	Name: Nxn 2\n\nObjectives:\n	
 Describe the prevalence of opioid overdose and impact on society.\n	Recogn
 ize the people who might be at risk for opioid overdose and how these pati
 ents present.\n	Discuss tips on how to prevent opioid overdose.\n	Describe
  the components of a naloxone training kit and its indications for use.\n	
 Demonstrate the use of naloxone training kit including intramuscular injec
 tion.\n\nView this event online: https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/1
 98844
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198844
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[C1] SPECIAL EVENT: WIHP Orientation Session: Sharing Circle Debri
 ef
DTSTART:20260901T200000Z
DTEND:20260901T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260903T235526Z
UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198871@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:\nCourse: MED 511\n\nInstructors:\n	Paulette Dahlseide (pdahls
 ei)\n	Taylor Turvey (turvey)\n\nMy Group:\n	Name: SC - Group D\n	Location:
  ED 165\n\nObjectives:\n	Reflect on the history and legacy of residential 
 schools and its impact on Indigenous health from survivors' perspectives.\
 n	Reflect on the conditions under which residential schools were operated 
 in Canada and the lasting impacts on survivors and family members.\n	Analy
 ze the philosophical assumptions that guided residential schools.\n	Discus
 s the impact of residential schools\, disconnection from family\, culture\
 , community and land.\n	Reflect upon the intergenerational trauma from the
  survivors perspective.\n	Describe the value of reconnection to culture\, 
 language\, land and community to improve patient care.\n\nView this event 
 online: https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198871
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198871
END:VEVENT
